"In today’s working world, we often need to communicate ideas to large audiences. This is usually done through oral presentations. Thus, mastering the art of the oral presentation is an important skill that can help one be successful in his or her profession. Audio and visual aids are two things that can be incorporated into an oral presentation. They are both great ways to enhance your presentation and make sure the audience clearly understands your main idea. For example, PC projectors can be used to show simple visual aids like graphs, charts or pictures on your topic. Try and keep it simple, though. Inundate your audience with too much information and you might confuse them. As the speaker, your words and ideas are what everyone comes to hear about. The presentation should only aid you and not be the primary focus; it shouldn’t be ALL about flashy computer images, and super detailed charts, even though they may help. If people leave your presentation remembering nothing but a bunch of graphs or leave blinded from staring at a white projector screen, chances are you didn't give a successful oral presentation.": "f41e56c66a6d",
