"Look at all the scary faces on the pumpkins. It must be Halloween. Making jack-o'-lanterns is a traditional activity this time of year. People use them to decorate their windows and front porches so that their house looks spooky.": "d1e02559d96f",
"Look at all the scary faces on the pumpkins. It must be Halloween. Making jack-o'-lanterns is a traditional activity this time of year. People use them to decorate their windows and front porches so that their house looks spooky. Making a jack-o'-lantern is quite simple and fun. All that is needed is a knife, a spoon and a candle. Start by cutting a lid out of the top. Cut it at an angle so that the lid will sit on the top and not fall in. Next, use your hands or a spoon to scoop out the seeds and guts of the pumpkin. When the inside is clean, you are ready to carve the face. Before cutting the face, first draw it on with a marker. This makes it easier to cut as you can just follow the lines. Be careful with the knife so that you don't cut yourself. The final step is to place a candle inside the hollowed out pumpkin. When the candle is lit, the eerie face will glow in the dark, casting an evil light on everything around. Place the jack-o'-lantern in a safe place where nothing will catch on fire. Also, blow the candle out before you go to bed or leave the house. When Halloween is over, don't forget to throw the pumpkin away or it will rot, stink and attract flies. Or you could make pumpkin soup for your family and friends.": "b97e00a758bb",
