"Putting in a drainage ditch by hand is a lot of work, but not if you know someone with a backhoe. With a backhoe, it is relatively easy to dig large holes as its long powerful arm is able to dig into the ground with ease.": "1c86205cef7e",
"Putting in a drainage ditch by hand is a lot of work, but not if you know someone with a backhoe. With a backhoe, it is relatively easy to dig large holes as its long powerful arm is able to dig into the ground with ease. At the foot of these steps, this hoe is digging a long, narrow ditch. However, before the hoe operator was able to begin digging, someone had to break up the concrete with a jackhammer. After that, the backhoe could start. The hoe operator sits on the large machine and uses the controls to move the machine around. He is very careful while working so that he doesn't do any more damage than is necessary. He also has to watch carefully for underground lines and pipes. To dig a hole, the operator extends the boom and opens the bucket. When the bucket touches the ground, he slowly closes it and moves the arm toward the hoe. This process fills the bucket with dirt. The arm is then raised as the machine turns. When the bucket is over the place where he wants to make a pile, he opens it again and empties the dirt. All this is done without actually moving anywhere, because the body of the machine rotates on its tracks. This process is repeated until you have a big hole or, in this case, a ditch.": "08ca47f2f0df",
