"Trucks, cars and buses are not always the most practical way to transport people from point A to point B. This is particularly true when point B is hundreds of meters up the side of a steep mountain. In such cases gondolas are much better.": "cb09d700f5c4",
"Trucks, cars and buses are not always the most practical way to transport people from point A to point B. This is particularly true when point B is hundreds of meters up the side of a steep mountain. In such cases gondolas are much better. Gondolas use heavy cables strung between poles to carry cars up and down mountains. Usually they run high above the tree line, giving you a bird's-eye-view of the surroundings. In the picture on the left, we can see passengers who have purchased tickets and are waiting to board the gondola running between Taipei Zoo and Maokong. After a long wait in line, the passengers are excited as they are finally preparing to board the gondola. The doors of the car open automatically. Once on, the doors close again and the car swings into motion. As you exit the terminal, the floor quickly drops away as does your stomach. Now all that is below you are trees and plenty of air as you climb steadily, onward and upward. It is very picturesque. You can also see other cars suspended in front of you. From this viewpoint, the world seems quite amazing. It is a rare opportunity to experience things dangling from such heights. In reality, our world is very two dimensional (other than climbing a flight of stares). The vertical is something that maybe only pilots and birds really navigate. If only for a moment, taking a ride on a gondola can give us a new perspective on the world around us.": "d7a7a9bfd768",
